WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.407
(band music plays)

00:00:02.407 --> 00:00:04.830
- Have you, have y'all met before?

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.010
- No, but I have this thing

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.538
where I have amnesia
with famous people, so I

00:00:10.538 --> 00:00:11.850
- We may well have. We have actually!

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.800
- I, we might have met
and if I see you again

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.060
- Wait, have y'all met?

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.380
- [Eddie] No, I don't really.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.330
But I'm so thrilled to
hear that you have amnesia

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.250
cuz I have like a brain like a sieve

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.210
and so
- [Emily] Yeah!

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.230
- I have exactly the same thing

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.340
and it's horrendously offensive

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.450
to people I've actually met.
- I know people get

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.710
very offended when you don't remember

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.300
and it's like, "Oh my God,
there's so many people

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.133
in the world.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:28.966
I'm so sorry."

00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:29.910
- It's like I think I have

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.280
like this thing where I hold people up.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.828
I met Seth Rogen and I was
like, "So nice to meet you."

00:00:34.828 --> 00:00:35.910
And he's like, "Well we met before."

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.140
And I was like, "Oh really?"

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.460
He's like, "Yeah, remember we met

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.230
at the audition for '40 year old Virgin?'"

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.560
And I was like, "No. Nope,
I didn't audition for that.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.090
I don't know what you're talking about."

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.150
And then it like three weeks
later I was like, "I did.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.817
I did audition for that movie."

00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:50.650
I complete-

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.340
And it's happened several
times, but I've been savvier

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.892
and just been like, "Yes, it
so nice to see you again!"

00:00:55.892 --> 00:00:56.755
- Exactly. To see you!

00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:57.817
- See you! To see you!

00:00:57.817 --> 00:00:58.650
That's, yeah.
- That's very helpful.

00:01:00.171 --> 00:01:01.410
Lovely to see you!

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.090
- Anyway, but I don't ever get offended

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.350
if you don't remember this moment,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.450
I will just not care.
- [Emily] I think I will.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.890
- Yeah. I'll be like, cool.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.000
Me neither.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.250
But your sister Zoe has been here before

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.800
and she said that you guys
grew up on sets, right?

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.633
On movie sets.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:17.670
- Yeah. My dad's cameraman
and my mom's an actor

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.310
and so we grew up going to visit sets.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.800
So I think the big motivator

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.200
for me becoming an actor
was visiting my mom

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.490
on set one day.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.004
- And there were donuts.

00:01:28.004 --> 00:01:29.311
- Oh. Craft service.

00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:30.533
- So, you know
- [Kelly] Yeah,

00:01:30.533 --> 00:01:32.363
for a kid, craft service.

00:01:32.363 --> 00:01:33.380
- I go with my plan since then.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.210
- The new show is called "Devil in Ohio."

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.030
I did, we were talking about
when we were watching the clip

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.130
how we just wanted to
bring the scariest shows

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:41.975
in one episode.

00:01:41.975 --> 00:01:42.808
(Eddie and Emily laugh)

00:01:42.808 --> 00:01:43.641
Like today.

00:01:43.641 --> 00:01:44.474
- Yeah, totally.

00:01:44.474 --> 00:01:45.307
- Like it was like we just went real dark

00:01:45.307 --> 00:01:46.140
- Creepy.
- for y'all today.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.190
- Yeah. Yours looks so creepy.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.091
- I know. Yours doesn't look not creepy.

00:01:49.091 --> 00:01:51.120
It's called "Devil in Ohio."

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.580
So what drew you to this role?

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.960
- Well, I've always had a fascination

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.109
with cults and so this deals with, okay.

00:01:57.109 --> 00:01:58.530
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.990
My character's a psychiatrist who,

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.930
there's a teenage girl
who escapes from a cult

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.900
and she ends up having a great
idea of bringing her home

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.840
to her family and having
her move in with her.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.870
And I've always had fascination with cults

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.910
but I also was like well, what would make

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.450
this psychiatrist decide
to bring home her patient?

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.425
So that's I guess where my fascination,

00:02:20.425 --> 00:02:22.320
that's why interest

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.940
in the show came from.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:24.773
I love it.

00:02:24.773 --> 00:02:26.010
I love the whole, I don't love cults.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.007
I don't, I'm not like into that.

00:02:27.007 --> 00:02:30.210
- You don't love cults?
- No, but hey,

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.190
but I love that like it's
something that draws you in

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.080
because at this point y'all
get to kind of pick what you do

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.250
and like what really interests you

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.083
and you love in your career.

00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:37.073
So it's fun to watch y'all.

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:38.540
- Aww.
- [Kelly] You're so gifted.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.390
- Is fun to watch you.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.437
- So things that got,
well, I don't do scary,

00:02:41.437 --> 00:02:44.820
but things that, they did
get creepy on "Bones" though

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.960
cuz you were always
around like dead bodies.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.983
Did you ever have to like, like he did,

00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:48.480
you know, went to study

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.313
as a nurse for a bit

00:02:49.313 --> 00:02:50.146
and apparently sucked, but

00:02:50.146 --> 00:02:50.979
(guests laugh)

00:02:50.979 --> 00:02:52.860
You don't want him around!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.080
But did you ever like
go like I don't know,

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.310
to a morgue, like when you did "Bones?"

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.143
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.710
We went to the coroner's office.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.600
But I didn't do it right
away when I started.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.470
I did it like a year or
two in, but yeah, that--

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.939
The smell!

00:03:04.939 --> 00:03:06.077
- [Eddie] Oh my gosh
- I was gonna say

00:03:06.077 --> 00:03:06.933
the smell has to be

00:03:06.933 --> 00:03:07.920
- Because we were dealing with fake bodies

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.050
so we got really used to the fake bodies

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:12.090
and we'd eat our lunch
over them and it's like

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:12.923
you're just used to

00:03:12.923 --> 00:03:14.820
like gooing up our hands.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.180
It was disgusting but we got
completely desensitized to it.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.399
But real bodies smell horrible

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:23.160
especially when they
decompose, apparently.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.890
And so that's the thing
that I stuck with me.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.270
I couldn't get outta my nose.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.100
- Nope.
- [Emily] It was scarring.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.080
- Nope.
- Did it change

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.827
like performance then?
- [Emily] No!

00:03:31.827 --> 00:03:32.870
- Did you go back and then you go

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.052
(Eddie loudly sniffs)

00:03:34.052 --> 00:03:36.570
- No, and that's what my choice
at the beginning was like

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:37.470
I don't think I need to do this

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.120
cause I think I'm
supposed to be comfortable

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:39.953
with these bodies
- Exactly!

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:42.270
- So I can just use my
imagination to pretend

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.103
that I'm comfortable.

00:03:43.103 --> 00:03:43.936
- You're an actor!

00:03:43.936 --> 00:03:44.769
- And that worked better.

00:03:44.769 --> 00:03:47.190
Then I had to like then use
my imagination even more

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.517
after going there to think like,

00:03:48.517 --> 00:03:50.220
"No, this is okay, this is normal."

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.053
Cuz it was.

00:03:51.053 --> 00:03:52.334
- That putrid smell is totally fine.

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:53.940
- Yeah, no it doesn't.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.080
I'm used to it.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.223
- Oh no.

